# a program's function of numbers called spaced, without parentheses, applies to each item too (guide 375)
'square := it * it; square [1 2 3]'	[1, 4, 9]
'square(x) := x * x; xs = [1, 2]; square xs'	[1, 4]
'square := it * it; square 3'	9
'twice(x) := x + x; twice "ab"'	"abab"
'f(x) := #x; f [1 2 3]'	3
